From c3d6f4346cded4c412b742996d128f814f176d28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel FORTE <gforte@wyplay.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:24:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] [Perf][Qwen4Exp] Vocab-truncated MTP draft head

Every draft token of MTP speculation runs compute_logits with the full
248,320-row lm_head: on sm_80 at the ~1.1 TB/s measured for these cards
that is ~1.2 ms per draft step of a ~19 ms iteration, 12-18% of decode
spent scoring vocabulary the model almost never emits. When the model
directory contains mtp_draft_vocab_ids.pt plus an
mtp.draft_lm_head.weight tensor (both produced by
benchmark/build_draft_vocab.py from the model's own outputs), the
drafter scores that small head instead and scatters the logits back
into full-vocabulary space with -inf elsewhere, so every downstream
path keeps its exact shape and semantics.

Output quality is unchanged by construction: the verifier is the
target model and never sees the draft head; an id outside the draft
vocabulary can only stop being proposed, never be wrong. Acceptance
may dip with vocabulary coverage; keep the id list counted from this
model's own generations.

When the draft head is active the full lm_head module is not created
and its checkpoint rows (shared_head.head / lm_head) are skipped at
load, returning ~1.27 GiB on the last pipeline rank.

Mechanism and the coverage lesson (a generic list covering 92% costs
~10% throughput; a counted list covering 97.5% does not) follow
syv-ai/HyperQwen's qwen3_5-mtp-draft-vocab patch, adapted to the
qwen4_exp MTP module. Opt out by deleting the two files.

Co-authored-by: Maki <agent@local>
